   210	### Coordinator rulings (binding)
   211	- **Entry seam with Movement 1 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 271 opens at Lowmarch with six; 118 marks; the released arm and mended ankle; Brom's shoulder still in the older healer's knot; the second wand at forty-one notches.
   212	- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY.** One use added: the Iron read in earnest on the bank at the landing on the 277th (the post's foot and the old sill), paid in near sight until the afternoon; logged twice. Pressure, Anchor and Wind were refused at the landing; Wind and the read refused in Lira's bout; Tide unused; Shadow held, twice and sealed; Oryn has not read Cael.
   213	- **Vastin** came over on the first boat on the 277th: a brown frieze coat, an ash stick, a bad knee, raw hands (the left does not open flat), a small purse; no age; **no Iron Wall shown** (he held the stern strap with a turn on a post, his boots and his back). He holds no office and nobody sent him. He has asked for a bed and for nothing else; he has not asked to join and nobody has framed him as joining. He sleeps in the loft over the tap.
   214	- **What Vastin added about the layer is exactly four things:** it cannot be reached (there is no key); a citation to a designer; the suppressed survey records; the technician's line. The layer's existence was Karis's already (her protected line stands unglossed, OWNER-pending #48). Nothing says that menders, technicians or any office know more; nothing says it has been tried.
   215	- **The three papers.** (1) **The records:** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather; six taped rows, a year to a row, of survey abstracts measured in lengths, knots and strides, with the dead surveyor's four-sign index printed at their heads; an **anomaly column** in which every sheet, in every hand, for six years carries the one word *Total* (an entry, not a sum; no figure); "More than four" (Karis, counting distinct sign-groups; she gives no number); the Fallow completion report is the last, loose sheet, and carries **five strokes for a name and a count of six** (locked Book 7 ch40, ch43), not five names. (2) **The page:** a COPY in Vastin's own hand of one line from an old register, carried in oilcloth in his coat: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". "The Architect" is a title, not a name, and a word Karis has never met in any stratum. It is never called a leaf; **the leaf has not appeared**. (3) **The technician's sheet:** the two protected lines with a date between them, a brush bar across what followed, and Karis's *not read*. **The date is a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and is never printed as figures** (the source gives none; no owner decision is needed). The office had filed the sheet at the end of the second row and it lies there again.
   216	- **Seln went still at the date** and said only "I have read it." He has not said the sum. Cael does not know what it was and has not read the date closely. **Nobody has connected the date to anyone**, and nobody has interpreted the sequence. "Classification event" is not defined.
   217	- **Speakers (protected):** "Archmarshal" is Cael's; "What follows you," is Lira's; "More than four." is Karis's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," is Oryn's (Karis owns the order to bed). The long table's close is verbatim. "Nothing that can cross the Line"; the rim of the Stair "is not mine".
   218	- **Karis's receipt** (unsealed, signed K.) is in Vastin's coat. Karis holds all three papers and her copy of the sheet. Seln's second wand (forty-seven notches, a hundred and forty-seven days) lies under the lamp; he will cut no more.
   219	- **Cael has not touched the page.** He will rule at the plank in the morning (the 278th), in daylight, and ask for hands. Nobody said *west* in the back room.
   220	- **Teague's spear** now has "he/his" on the page (OWNER-pending #59 stands as defaulted). Teague's wrist is unbound and unused; forty sacks of salt at the landing; whether he has left for the cold road is open.
   221	- **Lowmarch:** the mule's stool at the board's end (Oryn stands beside it); Pike's new cloth, Teague first, the five carried **eleventh** by place; Oryn's bench a yard past Pike's right-hand post; the first boat took people only; the hauling rope has two yarns gone and the stern strap is improvised; the sixty yards of cordage are still on the western bank and the rope debt stands; the hurdle is paid. Ephram's letter went west on the afternoon boat. **Purse: 118 marks.**
   222	- **Oryn's swallowed sentence** has now been shut in three times (the 268th, the 271st, the night of the 277th).
   223	- **Names:** none minted. **Length:** 30,105 after repair, against 30,000.
