    66	## What must remain true / withheld
    67	
    68	- **No wall drill with Teague's crew.** The doctrine "behind it" is told to them only on the pass morning.
    69	- The Compact knows the crew walks out declaring. **It never sees what works inside.** The watch sees bodies stand inside the line.
    70	- Teague is **not told** Cael took his Force. The Force is not used, only lined dry. "First use" belongs to the pass.
    71	- The two pages stay separate in every head. Never use *terminal*, *circuit* or *infrastructure*. "Recent administration" means **the Compact**. Nobody reaches for "someone else".
    72	- The cairn is on the 300th. Count Oryn's days from it (§12 C3). No cutaway at the court.
    73	- The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] and the older healer still do not speak to the six. The broad man's first word to them is "Aye", on the 305th.
    74	
    75	## What the author owns
    76	
    77	The leg's country, camps and weather. How the seep is solved. The watch's behaviour in detail. The crown's view. The blanket's order of work. The humour of two men on sticks at one fire who never mention it.
    78	
    79	## Where we leave pressure
    80	
    81	A notch in the hills to the east, low and square, where the bearing runs. Seln did not like it and will look again from nearer. Past it, by the office's distance, the oldest site waits. Cael wants it more than anything since he was fourteen, and he has told Karis why. He was right. He does not yet know how right.

