   525	- **The eleventh's lines** are set in italics, as Cael's own plain words for what stands in the place behind his eyes (the coordinator took them out of the fenced block; the frame sentence before them is unchanged).
   526	- **Small things.** Brom keeps a twist of cloth under his box's lashing with a roping needle and waxed thread. A pot of horse liniment was begged from the stable for his left shoulder. Vastin mended the becket of Cael's box with the stable's awl. The old keeper at the third gate did not write the lateness against the card on the 290th. The third tread of the cut's bottom flight is now out of its bed.
   527	- **Roles (all unnamed):** the carter's lad; two yard-men; the broker's factor; the under-registrar (spoken of); the watch; the six in hoods.
