   259	Cael went round to the basin with the pot.
   260	
   261	Seln was there before him.
   262	
   263	He stood at the water's edge with his hands in his sleeves and his back to the slab, looking down into the basin; and it was so exactly where he had stood on the two hundred and eightieth day that Cael's foot stopped of itself. He had been at that slab then, with a row of paper under his hands that counted a sheet short. He had looked up, and found a small grey back turned to him at the water. And when he looked down again there had been a sheet lying before him on the rock, which had not been there, with a registry year at its head and a day.
   264	
   265	He had laid that day against the first line of his own file. He had done it twice, a figure at a time.
   266	
