   285	*Two hundred and ninety-fifth day. The spring, a furlong south of the border road; nineteen miles and some from the gate. Out at first light by the outer arch: six out, as six in, and none of us written. Sixty yards of four-strand, two marks. A hundred and twenty-eight. The coil rides on the rope-walk's dray, with forty of its kind for the landing. So does Vastin, for a copper a day of his own; he walks the hills. Sixteen of thirty. Lira: thirty. She says that it is an arm.*
