    38	
    39	"Him that's first on the one-armed man's cloth. He's leather on his wrist." The slate was turned over, where a column of strokes stood. "He brought my salt up himself, behind the first of the carts, with three of his own. He asked me what I'd seen from that lip; and when I'd told him, he asked it again, which nobody ever did before. Then I said that I meant to keep the five that had done it, if silver would keep them. He said that they were for the east. He said I might offer, and welcome, and that I'd have it back in very nearly those words."
