/bin/zsh -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
from pathlib import Path
import re
base=Path('editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript')
corpus='\\n'.join((base/f'chapter-{i:02d}.md').read_text() for i in range(1,41)).lower()
words=set(re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]+(?:'[A-Za-z]+)?\",corpus))
units={
'43:71':'''But he stopped at the place, and so did Vastin, a stride behind him, and stood on it, and looked at the walls on either side, which were the same walls, and at the scree, which was not road and never had been, and said, Here, and Cael said it back.''',
'43:87':'''Vastin put the weight on the knee. He did it slowly, as a man does who has been told a month and is on the seventeenth day of it, and it held, and he stood a moment with the stick off the ground, which was the first time since the cut, and then put the stick down again, because Oryn was not there and he was not going to be the one to tell her he had done it. Two words, he said. Both of them ours.''',
'44:167':'''Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four. Your researcher's on it, because a wall counts who walks a site and not who swings, and she's the one who found the site. Healers don't go on a wall's count — yours is on a north road and mine won't thank you for putting her on it. Shares by count, whichever way the site pays, and I'll not argue the researcher's share, because I've read her map and she's the reason there's a site. Field's mine. I've had a crew at the top of that sheet three years and you've had one eleventh, and the wall's the wall, and I'll not pretend otherwise to be polite. The reading's hers. I don't read. If she says a thing's old, I'll take it that it's old, and I'll walk to it, and my crew walks where I do. And on the site. On the site it's whoever's nearest the thing that wants doing. You know that. You did it at a hall with two of yours down, and I read it off your face at a marsh before you'd priced it yourself. I'm not here because I like you. I'm here because there's a thing on that bearing thirteen crews have walked past for thirty years and one crew went and looked, and I'd sooner be at the front of that than read about it on a wall. Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more.''',
'44:195':'''The wall's still the wall.''',
'44:245':'''Then you know what it costs. Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice.''',
'45:43':'''A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's for. The one on a sheet says how old the thing is.''',
'45:155':'''Somebody laid them down in order.''',
'45:161':'''It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means.''',
'45:177':'''Oldest last. Then that's where we're going. Past the fourth. On the line.''',
'45:271':'''Nineteen days. Then it's eleven more. Stand there.''',
'45:281':'''I'm on my route. Seven holds north of here owe me a visit and I've walked four of them since the fork and there are three I haven't, and there's an old woman at Thornwater with a knee that held through the winter and a ladder she'll not stop climbing. That's mine. Nobody at this ford gets a share of it. Your bearing runs east. So does the road to the last three holds, for two days, and then it doesn't. I'll walk the two days because they're on my way. I'll walk further than that because there's a man on this bank with ribs I've been owed a reading of since a marsh, and because ten people are going into two places that stop Paths at a stride, and I've seen what that costs, and I'll not have it said I was a day north when it cost it. I'm not a recruit. I've never been one. I'm a stop on my own route, and the route's mine, and the day I have to turn north I'll turn north, and nobody at this ford will ask me not to, because the one who'd have the right to has already said he won't.''',
'45:287':'''Sixth chair. On my terms. Which are the only kind.''',
'45:329':'''You listened when it told you the second time. Once. Once is once more than I priced.''',
'45:375':'''It held in a cut. You stood on it. With the stick off the ground. You've done it once, and it was in a cut, and you did it because a cut was where it went and you wanted to stand on the place.''',
'45:379':'''Noted. That's new. It's a useful word. It's his.''',
'46:223':'''There's a thing we read in Treswick. About the marks. About him. You'd want it, I think. Or not. Is it a finding? It's a leaf. Older than the board. It says what the thing was built for. Then it's not mine. Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table. My table's for things I can put my hands on. Lie still when I say. That's still the term.'''
}
for k,s in units.items():
    toks=[]
    for w in re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]+(?:'[A-Za-z]+)?\",s.lower()):
      if w not in words and w not in toks: toks.append(w)
    print(k, ', '.join(toks) or 'NONE')
PY" in /Users/drive/fractured-path-monroe13
