editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-12.md:265:It was the third time. She shut it, as she had shut it at a board on the two hundred and sixty-eighth, and at the same board three days after; and the sentence, whatever it was, went back down with the others.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-08.md:139:The last of the shelf went on the two hundred and seventy-fifth day, in one piece as long as the landing, and after it the river began to rise in earnest.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-07.md:277:"I got it standing on a plate with half a hall looking. It was the best morning that I'd had. And he says that a civil man at a gate keeps it and gives me a slip." She beat a course down harder than it needed. "I'm not asking what you'll rule. I'm saying that I sat there and tried to mind, and I couldn't tell whether I minded. I've not stood on a floor for two hundred and seventy days. I don't know any longer what I'd be holding it for."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-06.md:3:They came down to Thornwater's ford in the forenoon of the two hundred and sixty-fifth day, and Cael did not at first know the place.

