books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-17.md:87:"Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four. Your researcher's on it, because a wall counts who walks a site and not who swings, and she's the one who found the site. Healers don't go on a wall's count — yours is on a north road and mine won't thank you for putting her on it." He did not look round at her. "Shares by count, whichever way the site pays, and I'll not argue the researcher's share, because I've read her map and she's the reason there's a site. Field's mine. I've had a crew at the top of that sheet three years and you've had one eleventh, and the wall's the wall, and I'll not pretend otherwise to be polite. The reading's hers." A tilt of the head toward Karis, who had not stopped at the plank and was already at the back room's door with the case. "I don't read. If she says a thing's old, I'll take it that it's old, and I'll walk to it, and my crew walks where I do."
