editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:334:- **"Four hundred years"** appears only in the record's voice (the leaf's head, given in Karis's single paraphrase) and at the fixed positions: Cael's pole-two sentence, the 298th log, the 305th close dialogue and the closing prose. Do not add uses.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:343:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; canon quotes or calls back these, or Book 9 inherits them)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:345:Tier A is quoted in the canon files (bible, ledger, series entry) or is a system notice. Tier B is wording from earlier books that this book quotes; it is binding from its own book. Tier C is fixed by the source architecture as closers or fixed lines; keep it verbatim, because Book 9's planning will read the source. Straight quotes and em dashes as in the source; italics are not wording.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:347:### Tier A — canon-quoted and system text
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:359:11. **Cleon's goodbye (S17):** "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:365:16. **The grade (S17):** "A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's *for*." … "The one on a sheet says how *old* the thing is." / "Somebody laid them down in order" / "It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means." / Teague: "Oldest last." … "Then that's where we're going."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:372:23. **Pike (S2; S17):** "What'd he do?" / "Nothing," Vastin said. "Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." And the 297th line: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:376:27. **The contract (S17):** "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall." / Force: "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:378:### Tier B — earlier books' wording quoted here (binding from source)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:389:### Tier C — source-fixed lines and closers (keep verbatim)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:405:- **S17 log:** "Karis cracked the grade. The sites are ranked by age and the bearing runs oldest-last — somebody laid them out in order, and the order runs into the deep edge, toward the first one they ever made. Second-tier's the fourth site, the one the Compact fenced. Third-tier's out past it, on the line, quiet for centuries. Teague's crew came after the thaw like he said — ten of us now, and he's still better at this than I am, and the ledger still says so. Two crews, one bearing, and a straightedge my guardian sent me because my grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. Turns out she was right about the line. Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Also: "Two words," … "Both of them ours." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:407:- **S20 close:** "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." / "And it's on the line." / "It's the *end* of the line. Oldest-last. Everything before it was practice, or maintenance, or — I don't have the word. This is the one that's been quiet since before quiet had a name." … "You still want to stand in the middle of it." / "More than I've wanted anything since I was fourteen." / "Why." / "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." [OWNER-pending #57] / He was right. He did not yet know how right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:412:- **Closing prose (S24):** "He had spent the whole year learning that the world was built to prevent him — four hundred years of tiers and registries and a machine that lit for everyone but him, all of it laid down so that what he was would never come again. And at the center of the first place they ever made, the oldest silence on the continent, the one built before there was a word for it, he had felt no exclusion and no prevention and no wall. He had felt at home. He did not have a word for that yet. But he knew, now, walking back out across a floor older than the system that had expelled him, that it was not an accident — that the place built to end him was the one place he fit — and that the difference between *the system was built to exclude me* and *the system was built to prevent me* had a third sentence past it, waiting, that he was not ready to write. Someone had made the pattern. He was, he was beginning to understand, the pattern. That was as far as he could say." [OWNER-pending #57] [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:416:## 11. Reserved truths and release limits for this book
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:436:## 12. Canon conflicts found in the source (with the edition's working ruling)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:439:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:441:- **C4 — The grandmother.** The universe ledger lists "Hesk's grandmother" as the owner of the straightedge saying. Book 7 edition chapter 60's note (chapter-60.md:67) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11] ("Your grandmother said…") and S17/S24 make her **Cael's** grandmother, Hesk's late wife. **Edition follows the prose.** The ledger line is a slip.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:456:## 13. Sequence locks — firsts and silences the expansion must not break
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:463:- **No Iron Wall is shown** before the cut (279th). No Force is shown in Cael's presence before the meadow cart (298th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:466:- **"Noted" adoption:** Vastin's first is the 298th (the grade); Teague's first is the 303rd (the crest); Oryn's "Everybody says that now" comes on the 304th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:470:- **The mule** goes north with Oryn on the 281st and returns at Millrace on the 298th. From the fork to Millrace the boxes are carried on backs (ruling 16).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:473:- **Karis cannot read the index as a grade** until the 298th. The leaf is not readable on the page before the seventh day of Cleon's week.
