52:## #34 — Breeze licence and publication (OWNER, 2026-10-03)
55:## #35 — B4 month arithmetic (coordinator flag, 2026-10-05; extends C8 / BOOK_MAP §11)
56:The edition's Book 4 calendar (closed M4: the Fiske bout ≈d141, Fiske's protected "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final.") puts the eleventh of Sowing (Cael's birthday, ≈d167) about sixteen days before the Copper final and the semester evaluation, which the plan dates in Reaping (inspection from "the twelfth day of Reaping"; the evaluation "the twentieth of Reaping"). Sixteen days cannot span from an eleventh to a nineteenth/twentieth of a different, ordinary-length month.
57:**DEFAULT in force:** the prose never states month lengths, which month follows which, or a day count between a Sowing date and a Reaping date; day counts are stated only in days/weeks from events. The protected Sowing/Reaping dates stand. Owner may later rule the series calendar (e.g. Reaping as the month after Sowing with a shorter feast-month between, or moving the birthday earlier). Does not block.
59:**#35 update (coordinator, 2026-10-05, B4 M5 review).** The plan's own protected lines collided: M4's "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final." (closed, published) vs the M5 closing Log's "Semester evaluation in nine weeks." Ruling: the Log now reads "seventeen days" (BOOK_MAP §9 amended). With the final on the nineteenth of Reaping and the evaluation on the twentieth, M6–M7's events fit the seventeen days (semifinal ≈ the tenth, nine days before the final; delegation the twelfth/thirteenth). The one residue is the birthday's month name: "the eleventh of Sowing" falls about sixteen days before the nineteenth of Reaping. The DEFAULT above stands (never state month order or a cross-month day count). Owner options: accept short months / an intercalary feast-week; or move the birthday to "the third of Reaping" (B5's recollection would follow).
64:2. **Track name.** B3 ch1:296 has the gate clerk say "observer track"; B2 calls it the "demonstration-provision track". **Default:** in B2 M8, Quenna or Cael uses both names once ("the demonstration-provision track; the observer track, on the gate list"). Book 3 is untouched.
66:4. **Season.** B3 ch1:136 says "Early autumn"; ch9 says the Reydan entry reached Karis "in the first days of autumn". The B2 map says "name no months; keep departure before hard winter", and the B2 M8 draft has frost on the departure morning and "before the first snow". **Default:** B2 ch60's departure morning names no season and shows no frost or snow. Quenna's warning becomes "before the weather turns on the hill road". Book 3 stands as written. The owner may later rule on the series calendar.
67:5. **Log format.** B3 uses four headings per fragment. B2 M8 begins that format with the Compression entry, and Cael means to redo the older three on the road. Accepted.
73:- **O1 Season names.** The series calendar is season-blind in Book 5: weather words only, and no month order (#35, #36.4).
74:- **O2 Cael's birthday.** It stays "the eleventh of Sowing" and is never set beside a season word. The owner may still choose "the third of Reaping" (#35).
76:- **O4 Weekday names.** House scheme: Halcenvane uses First-day … Seventh-day. "Tuesday" appears only in Daeva's window (Norhold/Auremont).
94:- **Bronze.** Rooke places Bronze across the top of the 22–27 band. The tournament does not bracket it; there are four brackets (Copper, Iron, Silver, Gold).
109:- **What is public.** Book 4's "two public" meant the Greyvane hearing transcript, which records Wind and the Iron read (plus a thin Ember exhibit). In Book 5 M4, Cael spends Ember's two contacts on the caravan captain on a public regional floor, at its documented rate.
115:  - Cael's inventory may say "the record holds two of them public… shown a third at its documented rate".
118:## 41. Book 5 tournament calendar re-dated after M6 (coordinator default, 2026-10-05)
119:M6 defers the exhibition ring (west-tower notice, T5); the ring is complete at dawn T11. New spine: Shield captain T11; duelist and Vastin's seat T14 (chair held thirteen days, replacing "nine"); rest day/birthday T15; team trial T16; filing T19; convening T20; third place T21; finals T24; closing T26. Recorded in book-05 BOOK_MAP §6 [M6-redated] and the M7 packet. Owner may restore a tighter span; the birthday date itself stays pending under #35.
123:- **Season-blind B6 (#19 vs #35/#37 O1):** #19's restructure keeps its SHAPE (one academic year; served on the eighth day; the cache and Vastin before the midyear recess; the ruling in the year's last month; the Line crossed after the year's close) but carries NO season or month names — "the year's first weeks", "the cold term", "the midyear recess", "the year's last month", weather words for texture. "December" is struck. Owner may restore seasons when the series calendar is ruled (#35, #36.4).
124:- **The birthday in B6:** a fixed date ("the eleventh of Sowing" default under #35; never beside a season word), with no cross-year day count and no month-of-year ordinal stated. The edition's own counts put the B5→B6 interval near 205 days, so the series calendar must later decide whether the academic year, the recess or the birthday moves. Owner item.
129:Book 5 closed with no Norhold session (C8), so Cael's file carries the Greyvane grant and TWO renewals on paper (the twentieth of Reaping; the mill town). Default in force: the protected B6 first pole stays verbatim; every non-protected count in the B6 plan states "two renewals on paper"; no interval sitting is staged. Owner options: (a) let the pole stand as Cael's rounding; (b) amend the protected line to "renewed twice" (the audit's recommendation); (c) stage the displaced sitting in B6 M1's interval log. Source: `book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md` §F (D12 = A11/C8).
132:The Compact's formal challenge (B6 ch5, Tier B first page) addressed "the enrollee of record, Cael, unclassified". Book 5 makes registry usage explicit: official instruments use *Caelen Hesk-ward* (B5 ch2:5; ch5:87, Karis: the tournament roster's line was "the first time any official paper has ever called him what we call him"). Default in force: amend the one noun phrase of Tier B text to *the enrollee of record, Caelen Hesk-ward, unclassified,* — the rest of the first page unchanged (Tier B permits recomposition where a word is wrong; this is a canon correction, recorded here). M2's house answer addresses the same name. Owner may restore "Cael".
134:## 45. Book 6 length — fuller later movements (OWNER RULING, 2026-10-10)
140:- **The book's last line and the six restored units** (Gault's last note; the personnel query; the waystation board; "You couldn't read me…"; Cael's reply to Daeva; the closing exchange) are verbatim from the protected wording, with only the edition's mandatory changes ("Since my Kindling"; "Nine fragments"; the personnel query's teaching-assistant role, calendar and house frame).
144:The protected Tier B minute reads "*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*" In this edition Gault is the evaluator of record and the Archmarshal's office is the certifying office that declined. **Ruling: the protected line stays verbatim and is read as the form's own mislabel** — an old column heading with no place for the right office — which the scene already dramatizes (four pens stop; Gault "had declined nothing"). One plain sentence was added outside the protected line so a young reader is told so directly: "The refusal was the Archmarshal's; the form's old column had only Gault's title to put it under." Owner may instead release the protected line and have it name the certifying office.
148:- **Season-blind and feet/yards, continued into Book 7** (as #37 O1 and #42 did for Books 5 and 6). Named seasons and metric units are replaced, minimally, INCLUDING inside Book 7's protected lines (for example "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." becomes "After the thaw. …"; "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." becomes the same distance in yards). Generic "season" and "month" stay. Every changed protected line is listed, old and new, in `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md`; the owner may restore any or all when the series calendar is ruled.
150:- **The birthday:** day 102 past the Line stands, never beside a season, a month order or a count back to the last birthday. By the edition's own day counts the two birthdays fall roughly 225 days apart (Book 6's mid-year, the year's close near day 207, then 102 days). The prose never states it; the series calendar remains the owner's to rule (#35, #42).
154:## 49. Book 7 — protected Quiet-line / Kindling wording (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 4)
155:Seven protected lines say variants of "mine didn't", "my Path", "mine has been asleep since I was fourteen", "dark since fourteen", "every Path … his had not". Edition canon (Book 6): Cael's own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and the Arbiter went dark; he has no Path. At a Quiet line the others' live Arbiters stop, his is dark before and after, and his fragments still answer. **Default until ruled: the protected lines stay verbatim**, the surrounding plan and prose state the canon, and the lines read as Cael's own shorthand. Options: (1) release only the conflicting clauses for a minimal canon repair; (2) release the affected log entries for clean re-composition; (3) keep as is (the default).
157:**#49 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 4).** Read closely, most of the seven lines already agree with canon as written: the first says the others' ARBITERS stopped and "Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen."; the fourth says "whatever I am isn't a Path"; Karis's struck line says "one dark since fourteen; no change either side of the line". Only two use "Path … mine" loosely ("Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't"; "every Path in this camp stops, and mine doesn't"). Default confirmed: all seven stay verbatim as Cael's log shorthand; Movement 4's packet carries a binding note that narration and dialogue never say "his Path" and state the canon exactly (the five live Arbiters stop; his has been dark since Kindling; the fragments still answer). If the owner prefers, only those two clauses need releasing.
159:## 50. Book 7 — "Six years I've wanted a face" (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 7)
160:The protected line gives Seln six years; edition Book 6 has him carry the case twelve years (fifteen in service). **Default until ruled: the line stays verbatim** and the plan stops calling the case a six-year matter. Options: (1) "Twelve years I've wanted a face."; (2) "All these years I've wanted a face."; (3) keep six and name a separate event six years back that began the wish.
164:## 51. Book 7 — "Tomorrow makes three" (OWNER ITEM; coordinator default in force, 2026-10-11)
171:- **#53 (needed before Book 8 Movement 4).** Protected "it took four years and a hearing to walk out". The plan itself notes the figure does not fit the academy span; #18 bars numbers for time since Kindling, and Book 7's first pole was amended on that ground. **Default:** verbatim, as Cael's rough spoken figure, never repeated as fact. Options: (1) the default; (2) release only "four years" for wording without a number, as was done for Book 7's first pole; (3) settle the series calendar so that it is true.
172:- **#54 (needed before Book 8 Movement 9).** The plan has the young member of Teague's crew named aloud once at his death. The edition has never named Teague's crew and no name is owner-approved. **Default:** no name is minted: the cry is narrated by its effect and the name's sound is not rendered. Options: (1) the owner supplies a name before Movement 9 (it then goes in the registry and the pronunciation list); (2) the default; (3) he stays unnamed even in-world.
173:- **#55 (needed before Book 8 Movement 9).** "Tell Lira's family I said so" (Cael's last letter to Hesk) still has no setup; this is #25, still open. **Default:** verbatim, no setup added. Options: confirm the opaque line; authorize one earlier setup beat; release or remove the clause.
177:- **#56 (Book 8 Movement 2 or 3, Thornwater).** `"Five months and twenty days."` — Lira's arm, from the Ring to its release. It is true on the plan's day count (day 96 to day 265–266) but only if a month is thirty days, and #35 says the prose never states month lengths. **Default:** verbatim. Options: keep; "A hundred and seventy days."; or a wording without a figure.
178:- **#57 (Book 8 Movements 8–9; extends #49).** Three protected lines speak of Cael's "Path" or say the machine never lit for him: `Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died.`; `His Path did not die. It also did not notice it should have.` (narration); `a machine that lit for everyone but him` (narration). Edition canon since Book 6: he has no Path; his own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, and it went dark. **Default:** verbatim; nothing else in the book says "his Path". The two narration lines are the hardest to square, since they are not Cael's own shorthand. Options: release the clauses for a minimal canon repair (Sol drafted wording, kept in the re-run report); or keep as is.
180:Applied under standing decisions, and listed old and new in `B7-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md` so any can be restored: Book 8's named seasons (#48) and its three "five years" counts since Kindling (#18), the same changes Books 5–7 made.
183:The source's Book 8 makes Teague's spear-carrier a tall woman throughout. The edition's locked Book 7 wrote this unnamed person as a man in five places (ch25:85 "a man with a spear"; ch51:357; ch52:45, :335, :337), because Book 7's plan never gave a gender and nobody caught it against Book 8. Book 8's protected text (§10) contains no gendered reference to the spear, and Book 8 Movement 1 uses no pronoun.
191:The protected unit (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 5) reads "Deep layer. Sequence initiated" [a Compact date] "Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —". The source prints no value either ("She gave the date. It was a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it"). Sol's plan audit asked for an owner-supplied date. **Coordinator default:** the edition does as the source does — the sheet shows a date in the office's reckoning and the page never gives its figures, in Movement 2 or at the spring in Movement 3 (where Cael knows it for his Kindling day; no span of years is computed, #18). If the owner wants a printed registry date, it has to be minted and reconciled with #35/#42 (the series calendar), and ch12 and the spring scene re-touched.

