    18	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 5 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two; purse 134 marks** at the end of Movement 5 (the night of the 290th). The eleventh, Iron-Wall-adjacent, came from Vastin in the alley's quiet minute; it did not fill, it *set*; its prompt is *This far?*; it has not been deployed and **Vastin has not been told** (Cael holds that as a debt he cannot yet pay; Lira has read the log). (2) **How acquisition lines are printed in this book:** the protected "Fragment eleven" and "Fragment twelve" units are CAEL'S OWN cataloguing of what he reads — set once, in italics, framed as his plain words; they are NOT printed as a system block and take no FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading or code fence. (3) **The Deepstacks:** an iron door with a sliding bar inside; twenty-seven steps in three flights of nine; three galleries. Middle gallery about 110 strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at its end, a shelf above it with a jar, a tied bundle ("Paper. Not stone.") and the black oak plank's sacking; the fifty-two sheets on three tables, 11/29/12; the plank stands against the third table. Eastern gallery: the old town's tall tally-books. One CARRIED lamp, Cleon's, held "a hand to the left" (Cael holds it and has begun to put it where the eyes are about to go). The boxes go up at the clerk's bell and come down each morning on a fresh card; the clerk writes *The same* and *four*. (4) **Cleon** knows Karis's name (he heard Brom say it and has used it once); his own is on the card and has never been said aloud. He has shown his Path from OUTSIDE only (bear / carried / nothing; "They're orders."; "Same make."; the limit: it does not work on a river, a man or a tree, and costs his eyes for an hour). **His week runs from the 287th to the 293rd.** He has not noticed Cael and knows nothing of the alley or the mechanism. (5) **Karis** has fourteen of twenty-three letters and reads numbers and number-words only; seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing; the bundle is tied and unread; Vastin's copied page is in her coat, unshown to Cleon. Her LEFT palm has seven stitches of Brom's under a strip of his shirt; she writes with the right. (6) **Vastin:** his right knee went again in the alley on the eleventh day of Oryn's thirty (a wall on it against her order, which he heard and asks that she be told); re-splinted with a slat from Brom's box, twice its size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He gave his name, rank and office aloud at the yard hatch on the 285th; nothing of it was written. He still knows nothing of what Cael carries. (7) **Brom:** the left (good) shoulder wrenched under a dray on the 286th and worse after the alley; he carries his box on the bound right shoulder, a debt entered for the mill's healers; the broker's offer (a guard's post inside the second wall) was answered "I'll think on it." and declined in fact. Lira: day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th; a bruised right shoulder; she drops from heights without the arm. (8) **Seln:** a registry clerk knows his face and voice (the price of a truthful answer at the hatch); he watches from the roof above the cut. His case is **SHUT** — never "unopened" (this edition's Book 6 opened it for the five) — and its contents are named nowhere in this book. He has seen one watcher three times (horseman's boots with the spur-rests cut away). (9) **The faction** (six, hooded, no faces, no Path opened) knows the loft and has shown that it knows; it saw Vastin's wall, a rock, a knife and a boy who stood still, and nothing of quiet ground or the fragments. Cael has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again. The loft is paid to the 295th.
    19	
    20	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 6 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two.** The twelfth is **Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** ("given, not taken"), acquired at his "There," on the 291st; it gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*), reads made things only, and costs the eyes afterward. Its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 6 and never reprinted. (2) **How it behaves:** it leans at every made thing, unbidden and OUTWARD, and Cael is learning not to look; it has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf, and **never turned inward**. He refused the inward turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first inward turn is unbidden, at Millrace, under Oryn's deep reading** (*still*, then *set*); the deliberate inward turn belongs to the plain's edge in Movement 9. (3) **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon. **Not Oryn (owed at the mill, with the readings round the place); not Vastin** (who also still does not know the eleventh or the mechanism). **Cleon's warning** ("If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — …") is known to Cael and Cleon only and is in no book; Cael tells nobody. (4) **The leaf** was read aloud once by Karis and heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; Lira, Brom and Seln read her copy; Oryn has not heard it. **Nobody quotes the leaf's wording again.** The reductions that may be said: *made*; *for a kind*; "the Architect" as a **title** (historical comparison only — "as old as the Architect" — never a present agent); "four hundred years" only where this packet's plan fixes it. (5) **The chronicle's line is marked and nobody speaks of it again**; the hole is never glossed. **Nobody joins the leaf to the lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; no *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*; no light, plate or instrument is said to attend, notice or want. (6) **Pole two was said aloud at the yard fire and is not in the log.** The line of march from it: "a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine" — "I want to stand in the middle of it." (7) **Seln's case is on his chest, shut, contents unnamed; he keeps it "a while longer".** Closed chapter 18 says he has carried it twelve years; print no other count. He will not follow the cut boots again and expects them on the road east. (8) **State at the night of the 293rd:** purse **130**; the reserve sealed in the third box; loft and handcart to the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman; Hesk's dividers and note shut in Hesk's book (never opened on a distance); Karis's fair copy in Cael's coat, the other in her notebook; the skin leaf under Cleon's jar and going to no counter; its back (a list of parts) unread — Cleon's work for the 294th. **Vastin: right knee day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**, slat-bound, stick, no kneeling, running or Wall; he sleeps in the stable's end stall and rides the handcart. Karis's left palm stitched (Brom's seven); Brom neither arm above the elbow; Lira day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd. (9) **Oryn** watched a Kindling at her fourth gate, is two days behind, will not come late to the mill, and means to read Cael "as deep as she went", asked first.
    21	
    22	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 1]
    23	
    24	- Read before drafting:
    25	  - Source `chapter-19.md` and `chapter-20.md`.
    26	  - Reviewer-only fourth-site evidence: closed Book 7 edition `manuscript/chapter-58.md:117–229` and Book 7 STATE_LEDGER AFTER MOVEMENT 8. The author does not open it under O3. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 26]
    27	  - The previous ending is this edition's `manuscript/chapter-46.md`.
    28	  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 32–35; §3 A (the Span; water at the seep), B 6, C (the leg); §5 (the Seln, Teague and Karis cutaways); §8 (the Span); §9; §10 Tier A 7–8, 14, 26 and the S19–S20 Tier C lines; §11; §12 C3, C14; §13.
    29	  - `STATE_LEDGER.md`, latest section.
    30	
    31	## Where we enter
    32	
    33	It is dawn on the 299th, at Millrace ford. There are twelve and a mule. Teague's wrist is wrapped. Vastin is on day 20. Karis is writing with the bound hand. Oryn's road runs east with them for a day and a half and then it does not.
    34	
    35	## What this movement is for
    36	
    37	The leg goes on the page as the place where two crews learn each other, and where the young one becomes someone a reader will grieve. Then the fourth site: a watch-post, a barricade, a captain's line, and a width that wins because the people inside the line have stood there before, with nothing gained by it. The thirteenth arrives. The next night every finding goes onto one blanket, the lamps finding is said aloud and filed on its own page, and a marshal finds a crack he does not pry.
    38	
    39	Consequential turns and promises:
    40	- **The leg (299th–303rd; ~9,000).**
    41	  - The Stair's bowl: Karis spends an hour at the rim checking a number she already has.
    42	  - **The cairn at noon on the 300th:** Oryn looks once, straight, and walks on east.
    43	  - The Hall's marsh, where Cael read himself twice earlier at the Hall. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 26]
    44	  - **Two dry camps, and water at the seep (~3,000 set piece).** Shale-backs stand on the slope by the only water. Teague's field reading leads. The young one moves too fast and the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] stops him with a hand, wordlessly.
    45	  - "Known" is entered under each date. The crest at dusk on the 303rd.
    46	- **The crest.** The watch-post: hut, fire, kit under a hide, two timbers, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." Seln: "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Teague: "Drawn?" Cael draws it. "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / Teague's **first "Noted."**
    47	- **The Span fight (304th; ~4,500, developed; BOOK_MAP §8).**
    48	  1. The watch has the first exchange. Brom takes bolts on Iron.
    49	  2. **Teague goes through the middle.** Cael is at his left, a stride back, the whole exchange. **The thirteenth.** The notice renders verbatim. The recoil goes to the wrist, then the elbow: "Through."
    50	  3. The watch reforms. **"Nothing was gained inside" is entered first.** "By count." Five go over stake thirty-four (Cael, then Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin) and four stay on the shelf. They walk. The pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east one at a time and is not pursued.
    51	  4. The broad man goes over the sink's edge at the fourth second, and Teague does not turn.
    52	  
    53	  **Win sentence, verbatim.** Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's week of colours.
    54	- **The Span itself (noon).** An arch on two piers over the sink. Carvings on the piers' inner faces, copied. No steps: the arch is walked as a road rises. The bearing runs "Through". **Nothing happens on the crown.** The thirteenth listens and the ribs know the cost. **The log, verbatim.**
    55	- **The shale camp (305th).** The blanket and its contents. The rows lean along the bearing. The point is fixed with a thumbnail circle.
    56	  - **The lamps finding, verbatim.** Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Vastin's third "Noted." **Cael does not add his own third page.**
    57	  - **The directive and the objection, verbatim.** "That's a crack." The seals are unnamed. "The Compact … Yes. Part of it."
    58	  - The broad man's "Aye". The healers' third exchange: one woman's hands in the other's work.
    59	  - **Force, dry:** Cael lines his frame on the shale without firing. The thirteenth listens and the ribs warn him.
    60	  - Seln on the pass: "I looked at it." **The close, verbatim.**
    61	
    62	**Physical challenge:** the seep, and the Span (a major fight).
    63	**Cutaways (~5,500):** Seln, ~1,800, on the crest at night or along the perimeter before dawn. He reads the iron and the watch. Seln's locked case stays shut and unopened. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 26] Teague, ~1,700, in the watch's hut after the fall. He counts his crew; the broad man's leg; the young one asleep. **Nothing of the mechanism. Not the young one's name.** Karis, ~2,000, the night after the lamps finding. She holds the refusal in her own head, knows the six-word sentence exists, and does not write it.
    64	**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Teague 2, the young one 2, Karis 2, Vastin 2, Seln 1–2, Oryn 2, Brom 1, Lira 1.
    65	
    66	## What must remain true / withheld
    67	
    68	- **No wall drill with Teague's crew.** The doctrine "behind it" is told to them only on the pass morning.
    69	- The Compact knows the crew walks out declaring. **It never sees what works inside.** The watch sees bodies stand inside the line.
    70	- Teague is **not told** Cael took his Force. The Force is not used, only lined dry. "First use" belongs to the pass.
    71	- The two pages stay separate in every head. Never use *terminal*, *circuit* or *infrastructure*. "Recent administration" means **the Compact**. Nobody reaches for "someone else".
    72	- The cairn is on the 300th. Count Oryn's days from it (§12 C3). No cutaway at the court.
    73	- The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] and the older healer still do not speak to the six. The broad man's first word to them is "Aye", on the 305th.
    74	
    75	## What the author owns
    76	
    77	The leg's country, camps and weather. How the seep is solved. The watch's behaviour in detail. The crown's view. The blanket's order of work. The humour of two men on sticks at one fire who never mention it.
    78	
    79	## Where we leave pressure
    80	
    81	A notch in the hills to the east, low and square, where the bearing runs. Seln did not like it and will look again from nearer. Past it, by the office's distance, the oldest site waits. Cael wants it more than anything since he was fourteen, and he has told Karis why. He was right. He does not yet know how right.

