editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:382:- Oryn (B7 edition `chapter-58.md:51–55`; `chapter-60.md:215,229`): `Find me at Thornwater.` / `Bring the map.` Her letter: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` / `Six, by letter.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:405:- **S17 log:** "Karis cracked the grade. The sites are ranked by age and the bearing runs oldest-last — somebody laid them out in order, and the order runs into the deep edge, toward the first one they ever made. Second-tier's the fourth site, the one the Compact fenced. Third-tier's out past it, on the line, quiet for centuries. Teague's crew came after the thaw like he said — ten of us now, and he's still better at this than I am, and the ledger still says so. Two crews, one bearing, and a straightedge my guardian sent me because my grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. Turns out she was right about the line. Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Also: "Two words," … "Both of them ours." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:462:- **Seln and Vastin exchange no words** before the 277th long-table doorway.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:463:- **No Iron Wall is shown** before the cut (279th). No Force is shown in Cael's presence before the meadow cart (298th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:65:- **Letters:** received Hesk's brass/note and Oryn's bark. Sent west on day 130: Hesk and Vell (`The session still stands`), plus the clerk's packet. Ephram's reply is deferred to the first boat of the thaw.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:127:- **Thornwater, days 265–266:** Lira's arm released (OWNER-pending #56 "Five months and twenty days.", said by Lira); **Lira asks and Oryn mends the ankle** ("Lie still," Oryn said; "Thank you." said by Lira; "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."). Before this Lira had asked once, on the mountain in Book 7, and nobody since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:174:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. She released the arm only when Lira took it; mended the ankle; answered Lira's thanks with "Route's whole… The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."; left the shoulder to the woman who tied it. She has seen the map with four rings and the line ("That's a line.") and has been told of the fourth site: twice the size, fenced, unentered. She has been told of the cord and the edges. **She has not read Cael** and has said that she will know what she is reading for before she does. At the word *station* she shut her mouth on a sentence and said nothing. She did not sit in the sixth place. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:180:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand** (96 − 20 for the cold stay; + 40 for the fence; + 5 for the roof; − 3 for the mule's shed). The reserve sealed and unopened. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, wanted with the first boat; one reed hurdle; a letter to Ephram. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. Both brass edges are in their cloths.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:202:- **Money, board, debts, and letters:** 118 living marks; sealed reserve untouched; eleven completed Pike lines; cloth still eleventh; sixty yards of four-strand rope owed for the first boat; one reed hurdle owed; Ephram's letter still due on the first boat; mule's cold-term shed fee paid (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:271`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:295-299`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-219,281-283`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-91`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:203:- **Fourth site and knowledge perimeter:** still unentered, unnamed, and untested; no sheet; no theory; nobody outside the six knows the mechanism, the instrument anomaly, or Karis's case (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-201,227-275`). The Compact response cannot have crossed the shut river before the day-277 ferry (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:99-103`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:233-241`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:208:## AFTER MOVEMENT 2 — chapters 7–12, days 271–277 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:212:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY.** One use added: the Iron read in earnest on the bank at the landing on the 277th (the post's foot and the old sill), paid in near sight until the afternoon; logged twice. Pressure, Anchor and Wind were refused at the landing; Wind and the read refused in Lira's bout; Tide unused; Shadow held, twice and sealed; Oryn has not read Cael.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:213:- **Vastin** came over on the first boat on the 277th: a brown frieze coat, an ash stick, a bad knee, raw hands (the left does not open flat), a small purse; no age; **no Iron Wall shown** (he held the stern strap with a turn on a post, his boots and his back). He holds no office and nobody sent him. He has asked for a bed and for nothing else; he has not asked to join and nobody has framed him as joining. He sleeps in the loft over the tap.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:221:- **Lowmarch:** the mule's stool at the board's end (Oryn stands beside it); Pike's new cloth, Teague first, the five carried **eleventh** by place; Oryn's bench a yard past Pike's right-hand post; the first boat took people only; the hauling rope has two yarns gone and the stern strap is improvised; the sixty yards of cordage are still on the western bank and the rope debt stands; the hurdle is paid. Ephram's letter went west on the afternoon boat. **Purse: 118 marks.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:222:- **Oryn's swallowed sentence** has now been shut in three times (the 268th, the 271st, the night of the 277th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:230:- **The first boat (flag):** first light on the 277th; eight passengers (a man with a ledger who carries the bag; two carters; a woman and a child; a drover; a lad; Vastin) and no goods; **the cordage stays on the western landing**. The bag had eleven pieces and none for the five. After noon she goes over again with twelve carters on foot, the bag and Ephram's letter; still no wheels.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:236:- **Teague (flag):** the wrist was unbound on the 272nd, a hundred and twenty-four days after it was bound. He has forty sacks of salt for the first boat and sees it over himself; then the block on the second ledge of the cold road. He did not put a day in his term; if the six are gone when he comes down, Cael is to leave word with Pike. The tall man has put the steel back on his pole.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:238:- **Ephram's letter (flag), sent on the 277th:** *Ephram. You lose because you run it alone. I lost to a seven-foot pole all the cold term, three to none and then three to one, and each time somebody on a bench told me what I'd done before I had wiped the snow off. Find a bench. Tell Rooke the yard out here is quieter too. He'd not say it was worse. — C.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:250:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventy-seventh day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 271, 272, 273, 275, 276, 277; Vastin's window, 265–276. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:254:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: thirty** (the read on the ground at the landing, the 277th). Shadow used twice in all and shut; held at dusk on the 272nd and the 277th. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else; he did not ask to read the knee. **The still place** has not been read, touched or named. He has not touched the cord or either brass edge for a hundred and nine days; the ruling is *hold*. His near sight went at the landing and was back for print by the afternoon. **He has not ruled.** He will say it "at the plank in the morning, in daylight" and ask for hands. He has not touched the copied page; his hand lay a hand's width from it for the whole of a lamp. **He has not read the technician's date**: he was at the table's far end; he knows that it is a registry year and a day, and that it is the line at which Seln stopped; he chose not to go up the table and read it. He lost the bout to Lira, two touches to three. He has written to Ephram. He kept back his own question to Vastin (why the second reading was declined). He has told Vastin nothing of what he carries.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:258:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration; no grey at the landing. **Right shoulder still in the older healer's webbing**; she pressed the knot on the 272nd and went away. He shored the post with a timber on the left shoulder. He has the purse; a hundred and eighteen. He roped the three boxes for carrying on the night of the 277th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:283:Packet 003 already carries day 278, the clearance slip, Vastin at the door end and not on the sheet, the silent drill, the cut, the spring, the date sum, the fork and days 279–281 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–38`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:300:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY-TWO**, both on the 279th at the cut: one grain of Ember at the mark (thirty-one; the heat came home along the left arm) and one Wind burst **away**, ten strides, to the north bank inside the wall (thirty-two). Pressure, Anchor, Edge, Storm and the read refused there. Shadow held, twice and sealed; Tide unused; no self-reading; Oryn has not read Cael. **Ten fragments: nothing came of standing two feet from the wall; the eleventh has not come.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:301:- **The cut (the author's staging stands; BOOK_MAP §8 allows it).** A hundred strides, a stride of ice down the middle, scree on the south, a low north bank, the sink fifty-five yards below it. Eight hounds (five seen, three hidden). The den had learned the road: it runs to where a declaration ENDS. Karis, Oryn and the mule were at the foot; Vastin, a stride behind Brom, stepped out and **declared Iron Wall** — a plane across the road from a line struck with his stick, wall to wall, two feet from Cael, rooted (he may not lift a foot), loud, spending him to the floor. Brom's rock (twice), Lira's knife with the left hand holding, Seln in the heap; five dead; **three went through the rotten ice of the sink and did not come up**. Costs: Brom's right foot (two toes, ten days from the 279th); **Vastin's right knee** (four holes shut by Oryn after "May I?" / "Yes"; the joint bound with laths; **a month** from the 279th: stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall). Karis's sixth line: *It goes to where a declaration ends, if it has learned that the declaring moves.* Twenty paid; **purse 138**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:306:- **The fork (the 280th evening; the 281st).** Oryn: "I'm not an archive person."; her past (a house for the sick in a city inside the Line; the column for the patient's tier; a woman from the river sheds whom she mended off the sheet; she walked out of a gate and has not been through one since — the author's, kept); "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second."; Seln's "Three weeks"; **the station term, written in the log and read back (verbatim)**; she priced all six, Vastin as long as the rest; "That's on me. It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." (the reading she has not given Cael); "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it."; "Not the steps," … "Not the square." She went north with the brown mule, her linen and the crossbow with its one bolt: five gates, the ford, Millrace in three weeks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:317:- **The slip and Pike's rule.** The clearance slip came over in the bag on the 277th; Pike drew a road between two heaps beside it. Twenty, "at the hold's own gate, on the factor's thumb, when the factor's walked it". **Pike will not write a clearance taken until a healer is said** (his own rule since his second year, when one of a crew of four bled for two days on a hurdle). His sixth line: *And a healer; of her own road; at her own price.*, the first column he has had for Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:345:**Calendar.** A little before noon on the **two hundred and eighty-first day past the Line**, going down the western side of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. Days on the page: 278, 279, 280, 281. No season, month or weekday name; no figures for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:353:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey at any point. Right shoulder still in the older healer's knot (if it tells him anything he is to put the load down and leave it down). **Right foot: two toes bruised, bound; ten days from the 279th, eight left on the 281st.** One box on the left shoulder. He has the purse and Pike's thumbed slip. He lays seven bowls and will carry Oryn's empty.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:359:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. On Pike's slip as its healer. She asked Vastin and had an explicit yes; shut four holes; bound the joint; two fingers on his wrist. She has priced all six and given Vastin as long as any. **She has not read Cael**: "It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." She has told the house, the column and why she left, and will not say where. She has her term in his log and has read it there. Gone north with the mule, her linen, and her crossbow with its one bolt; five gates, the ford, then Millrace in three weeks. She does not know that Vastin is carrying the kit's case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:361:**Vastin.** No office; **no age stated**. **Iron Wall declared once, on the 279th, in the cut**; spent to the floor. **Right knee: bitten, shut, bound stiff; the 281st is the second day of thirty**; on the stick; no kneeling, running or walls. He qualified every instruction. **He has not sat in front of the crew since the cut.** **He carries the tarred kit case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two) on the shoulder above his sound leg, taken up unasked at the fork-stone after Oryn had gone, and has told Cael so.** **He walks beside Cael from the top of the rise.** He said the town's name at the spring, the first to say it since the page. He knows the four hands, the doctrine and where a post stands. He has heard the daylight reading whole. **He does not know that the date means anything to anybody**, the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, or what is under the bar; nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:383:- **Oryn:** she and the brown mule are north of the fork on the reverse circuit; she has her linen and crossbow with one bolt. Her stated route is five gates, the ford and Millrace, where she expects the six in three weeks; she still owes Cael the proper reading and expects “all of it” from the archive (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:63–81,171–219`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:468:- **Who is below.** Inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with Cleon at the stair head; the unnamed clerk and his lantern remain outside. Seln is above ground, not on the 284th card or count, positioned to see who comes to the door. Oryn and the brown mule are at the second unnamed gate north (`ch25:87–117`; `ch26:183–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT:101`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:563:- **Cleon's knowledge and statements.** Cleon knows Karis's name and has used it once; he knows the hand, has externally demonstrated bearer/carried/ornament and “orders,” has stated both limits, has matched the same make, and has delivered the documentation/built-twice close. His week runs from the 287th through the 293rd. He has not noticed Cael, learned of the alley, shown the inside/lean, or acquired knowledge of the mechanism (`chapter-27.md:187–199`; `chapter-29.md:193–289`; `chapter-30.md:253–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:117`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:566:- **Karis.** Left palm has a long shallow cut and seven stitches, bound in a strip of Brom's shirt; she writes right-handed. No healer inside the gate has seen her. She has three days left of Cleon's week (`chapter-33.md:63–125,277,305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:111`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:569:- **Inn, purse, count and day.** Six are in the long loft over the stable; it is paid through the 295th, with pot at dusk and seven bowls. Purse 134, reserve sealed in the third box. The below-ground daily count remains Karis as bearer plus four hands; Seln is never one of them. Night of day 290 is complete; Movement 6 opens day 291. The cut will not be climbed at dusk again, but no further route ruling has been made (`chapter-31.md:265–267`; `chapter-33.md:277–305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:101–103,123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:670:- **Fragments and knowledge.** Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two. The eleventh remains unused and known to Lira through the log but not Vastin. The twelfth is known to Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon; Oryn and Vastin have not been told. Cleon knows how this one fragment came but no other acquisition history. The warning is known only to Cael and Cleon and is in no book (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:197–239,279–339`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:15–63`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:219–227`). **Coordinator ruling (overrides the audit here):** the twelfth leans at made things UNBIDDEN and OUTWARD in Movement 6 (the board, the rope-walk, the bridge, the dividers, the inn table), and Cael is learning not to look; a few unmeant outward glances are on the page and are not counted as deployments. It has never been turned INWARD, and he refused that turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. Movement 7's beat is the first INWARD turn, and it comes unbidden.

