+42. `manuscript/chapter-45.md`
+   old: `"I can tell you what the form is, which is very nearly the only thing that I am good for. Where an office makes a return of the same matter in every year, each sheet is numbered from the first that the office holds. The number is carried forward by whoever draws the next, and nobody is obliged to ask where it began." He stopped. "I have signed a great many returns with such a figure in the corner. I never once read it. I say what the form is; I do not say who drew the first."`
+   new: `"I can tell you what the form is, which is very nearly the only thing that I am good for. The first sheet dates the matter the office has begun to hold. Later returns carry that first date forward." He stopped. "I have signed a great many such returns. I say what the form is; I do not say who drew the first."`
