+20. `manuscript/chapter-43.md`
+   old: `It was the factor. There was the leather apron, and the slate on its cord, and the pair of pale eyes that had gone along six people and a healer at a gate and counted them. They counted now. They went from a quiet man, who had come up level with the cobs, to four with loads; and they rested last upon the tail-board, where a pair of raw hands lay on an ash stick.`
