+6. `manuscript/chapter-42.md`
+   old: `The keeper in undyed grey sat on his high stool with the frame on his knee. He looked at feet, and wheels, and hooves, as he had looked at them thirteen days before, and his thumb moved the beads: eight hooves, and four wheels. He came to the boots, and Cael counted five pairs with him. The thumb went on to the tail-board, where a pair of boots hung that did not touch the ground, and it stopped.`
