+   old: `Cael did the sum, since it was there to be done, and it was not a hard one. A sheet a year. Somebody had measured the place behind that fence, from eight points, with a cord, and written that the instruments read true and that the anomaly was total; and somebody had done so in every year for longer than any registry clerk now living had been alive, or his father, or his father's father. Six rows of it lay on this table, and the others stood in a drawer.`
