+The eastbound distance record also reverses the closed westbound road correctly. Closed day 278 puts the halting-ground eleven miles from the river (`chapter-13.md:205,261`); the 297th log returns eleven miles to Lowmarch (`chapter-44.md:205`). The ledger fixes landing→halting at eleven, halting→cut at nine, cut→spring at four, spring→fork at six, and the rise at a mile and more (`STATE_LEDGER.md:321`); the draft gives thirteen miles from spring through the cut to the halting-ground (`chapter-43.md:5–7,133,191`) and nineteen miles from the gate to the spring (`chapter-42.md:125–235,285`). No interval conflicts with Movements 3–4. The later “three days past the iron, a little less” is also compatible with the 306th–308th movement (`chapter-45.md:149–151`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:79–81`).
