+
+35. `manuscript/chapter-44.md`
+   old: `Cael saw it from the bench under the great ash as soon as there was light to see by, on the two hundred and ninety-eighth day, when the meadow was grey and forty fires were being blown up out of their ashes. It was a salt cart, with a pair of mules, and it had been drawn onto the grass at dusk by a carter who did not know how soft three weeks of thaw had left that corner. It stood now with its near wheels sunk to the axle. Half its sacks lay on the turf beside it. The carter had the mules out and was standing with his cap in his hand.`
+   new: `Cael saw it from the bench under the great ash as soon as there was light to see by, on the two hundred and ninety-eighth day, when the meadow was grey and forty fires were being blown up out of their ashes. It was a salt cart, with a pair of mules, and it had been drawn onto the grass at dusk by a carter who did not know how soft the thaw had left that corner. It stood now with its near wheels sunk to the axle. Half its sacks lay on the turf beside it. The carter had the mules out and was standing with his cap in his hand.`
