+
+4. `manuscript/chapter-42.md`
+   old: `"There's a tail-board. It's a copper a day to sit on, and you'll get down for every hill; I'll not have my cobs pull what can walk. And you'll hold your tongue on the moor. I'll not need to tell you why."`
