+5. `manuscript/chapter-42.md`
+   old: `He counted the copper into that brown palm, and it was kept. Cael saw the old shoulders ease by the width of a finger. It appeared that this road, at least, was going to take his money.`
+   new: `No copper passed. The old man put both hands on the stick. It appeared that this road, at least, was going to take the walking from him.`
